[
  {
    "ods": 0,
    "page": 2,
    "section": "G20_2024_1_Abstract",
    "arguments": [
      "The G20 is an important international forum to promote the implementation of the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development.",
      "A major obstacle to sustainable development worldwide that has so far received little attention are negative international spillover effects.",
      "All countries, and especially the G20 given their combined economic weight, must better understand, monitor and manage their spillovers to allow all countries to meet the SDGs."
    ],
    "source_file": "G20_2024_ArgsSGD0_llama3.3-70b.json"
  },
  {
    "ods": 0,
    "page": 3,
    "section": "G20_2024_2_Diagnosis_of_the_Issue_Addressing_Negative_Spillover_Effects_for_SDG_Achievement",
    "arguments": [
      "At the Agenda’s midpoint, however, the world is substantially off track.",
      "Therefore, at the SDG Summit in 2023, heads of state called for accelerated global action towards sustainable development."
    ],
    "source_file": "G20_2024_ArgsSGD0_llama3.3-70b.json"
  },
  {
    "ods": 0,
    "page": 4,
    "section": "G20_2024_2_Diagnosis_of_the_Issue_Addressing_Negative_Spillover_Effects_for_SDG_Achievement",
    "arguments": [
      "Addressing spillovers thus becomes crucial for ensuring that domestic progress in achieving the SDGs is not realized via externalizing negative effects abroad."
    ],
    "source_file": "G20_2024_ArgsSGD0_llama3.3-70b.json"
  },
